{"entities":"[{\"text\": \"Trimethoprim\", \"id\": \"D014295\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"hemolytic anemia\", \"id\": \"D000743\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"acute leukemia\", \"id\": \"D015470\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"anemia\", \"id\": \"D000740\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"hemoglobinuria\", \"id\": \"D006456\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"hemolytic anemia\", \"id\": \"D000743\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"trimethoprim\", \"id\": \"D014295\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole\", \"id\": \"D015662\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"sulfamethoxazole\", \"id\": \"D013420\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"anemia\", \"id\": \"D000740\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"anemia\", \"id\": \"D000740\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"hemolysis\", \"id\": \"D006461\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}]","filtered_entities":[{"text":"Trimethoprim","id":"D014295","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"hemolytic anemia","id":"D000743","label":"Disease"},{"text":"acute leukemia","id":"D015470","label":"Disease"},{"text":"hemoglobinuria","id":"D006456","label":"Disease"},{"text":"trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole","id":"D015662","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"sulfamethoxazole","id":"D013420","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"hemolysis","id":"D006461","label":"Disease"}],"head":"sulfamethoxazole","head_id":"D013420","pairs":[{"head":"Trimethoprim","tail":"hemolytic anemia","head_id":"D014295","tail_id":"D000743"},{"head":"Trimethoprim","tail":"acute leukemia","head_id":"D014295","tail_id":"D015470"},{"head":"Trimethoprim","tail":"hemoglobinuria","head_id":"D014295","tail_id":"D006456"},{"head":"Trimethoprim","tail":"hemolysis","head_id":"D014295","tail_id":"D006461"},{"head":"trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole","tail":"hemolytic anemia","head_id":"D015662","tail_id":"D000743"},{"head":"trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole","tail":"acute leukemia","head_id":"D015662","tail_id":"D015470"},{"head":"trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole","tail":"hemoglobinuria","head_id":"D015662","tail_id":"D006456"},{"head":"trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole","tail":"hemolysis","head_id":"D015662","tail_id":"D006461"},{"head":"sulfamethoxazole","tail":"hemolytic anemia","head_id":"D013420","tail_id":"D000743"},{"head":"sulfamethoxazole","tail":"acute leukemia","head_id":"D013420","tail_id":"D015470"},{"head":"sulfamethoxazole","tail":"hemoglobinuria","head_id":"D013420","tail_id":"D006456"},{"head":"sulfamethoxazole","tail":"hemolysis","head_id":"D013420","tail_id":"D006461"}],"relations":["D014295 | D000743","D014295 | D006456","D014295 | D006461","D015662 | D000743","D015662 | D006456","D015662 | D006461"],"result":"~","tail":"hemolysis","tail_id":"D006461","text":"Trimethoprim-induced immune hemolytic anemia in a pediatric oncology patient presenting as an acute hemolytic transfusion reaction. A 10-year-old male with acute leukemia presented with post-chemotherapy anemia. During red cell transfusion, he developed hemoglobinuria. Transfusion reaction workup was negative. Drug-induced immune hemolytic anemia was suspected because of positive direct antiglobulin test, negative eluate, and microspherocytes on smear pre- and post-transfusion. Drug studies using the indirect antiglobulin test were strongly positive with trimethoprim and trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole but negative with sulfamethoxazole. The patient recovered after discontinuing the drug, with no recurrence in 2 years. Other causes of anemia should be considered in patients with worse-than-expected anemia after chemotherapy. Furthermore, hemolysis during transfusion is not always a transfusion reaction.","metrics":{"precision":0.16666666666666666,"recall":1.0,"f1":0.2857142857142857,"rel_tp":1,"rel_fp":5,"rel_fn":0}}